FUNCTION "GLUE SCALE LOGIC" : VOID
TITLE =Glue Scale: DP Read, ASCII Parse, Pump Control, Alarms, KWS CY30   FC155
// History (full blow-by-blow in git log, this comment block was
// trimmed after it grew past STEP7's title/comment size limit and
// started failing to compile - "Byte offset/number too big" at the
// VERSION line. Keep future entries short.):
//
// v0.11-v0.14: simplified the ASCII parse loop (indirect addressing,
//   replacing 7 hand-unrolled digit blocks), added scale-fault sentinel
//   detection (NegativeUnderScore_Value), HMI alarm reset, REAL->INT
//   conversion for weight/setpoints.
// v0.15-v0.17: HMI DB (DB10) bridge - setpoints, live weight,
//   transfered-weight calc, bottomer-velocity mirror, drove the real
//   pump output.
// v0.18-v0.19: Valve_Open renamed Pump_ON throughout; overfill/underfill
//   now interlock the pump; added lamp scan pattern and alarm lamps.
// v0.20-v0.21: added PlatformMinWeight_SP sanity check and an
//   unconditional scale-fault pump interlock. Confirmed scale-fault
//   sentinel is INT -20663.
// v0.22-v0.25: folded FC156's power-up-calibration logic in here;
//   recalibration powers the scale off first; fixed real STEP7 compile
//   errors (jump labels, RED_LED/GRN_LED -> _Pnl, header size); fixed a
//   missing SET; before S/R coils reached via jump (RCS1/RCS2/RCS3/RCS5,
//   LSRS); adopted Michou's VAR_TEMP renames, "Update" network, and
//   WHT_SWL_1/2/3 -> _Pnl.
//
// v0.26: switched every classical timer (SD/T-number) to SFB4 (IEC
//   TON), per Michou: "Timers don't start!!! What about using SFB4
//   instead?" Two real bugs: (1) "SD" is S_ODT, the NON-retentive
//   on-delay - this project's comments wrongly called it "stored" all
//   session; the real stored one is "SS". (2) SFB-family timers are
//   call-driven, not hardware-autonomous like classical S5 timers - they
//   only advance while their CALL executes that scan with IN=1, so a
//   "start once, check two steps later" pattern (the old T53/K1 hold)
//   silently stalls. Fix: one "Timers" network computes every timer's IN
//   fresh and CALLs every instance unconditionally, every scan,
//   regardless of which step is active - still true in v0.27 below.
//   7 separate top-level SFB4 instance DBs (DB106-DB112) at this point.
//
// v0.27 changes vs v0.26 - SFB4 itself failed to resolve on this CPU
//   (compile log, 2026-10-02: "Symbol PT not found in symbol table" /
//   "FB requires the specification of an instance DB" for every SFB4
//   call - SFB2/3/4 aren't firmware-native on every S7-300 CPU; this one
//   needs the IEC Timer library FB instead, which Michou imported as
//   "TON"). Per Michou's own design ("why not call all SFB4 inside an FB
//   with it's own instance db, then call it once in FC155?"): replaced
//   the 7 top-level instance DBs with FB555_IEC_TIMERS.awl, one FB that
//   wraps all 7 "TON" calls as multi-instance children, called ONCE here
//   with one instance DB (DB106 "IEC_TIMERS_DB", reusing the number the
//   old TON_UNDERFILL DB freed up). Same "call every scan, IN recomputed
//   fresh" logic as v0.26, just targeting one CALL instead of 7; reads
//   "IEC_TIMERS_DB".<name>_OUT downstream instead of "<instance>".Q.
//   Caught and fixed one bug while integrating: FB555's own
//   TON_UNDERFILL call had PT wired to #LAMP_IN_TIME (copy-paste
//   leftover) instead of #UNDERFILL_IN_TIME - see that file's own
//   changelog.
//
// v0.28 changes vs v0.27 - corrected the power-on/calibration sequence
//   itself, per Michou (2026-10-03): "Mixed up in KILOTECH Pulses!
//   Process 'ON': When Power on K2 (500mS), K1 has to be on too! and
//   last 5sec! Now for recalib: Need to turn off: K2 alone 5sec, Wait
//   3 sec Then Process 'ON'!" Supersedes v0.22-v0.27's sequencing:
//   - "Process ON" (new, named, reusable step): K1 and K2 now start
//     SIMULTANEOUSLY (K2 500ms pulse, K1 stays on 5s flat) - previously
//     K1 started one step before K2's pulse, not simultaneous.
//   - Recalibration's power-off step is now 5s (RC_K2OFF_IN_TIME),
//     not 3s - K2 alone, no K1 involved at all at this stage (unchanged
//     from before, just the duration was wrong).
//   - NEW step: a 3s dwell with nothing active, between the power-off
//     and Process ON - repurposes the PWRON_IN/PWRON_IN_TIME/PWRON_OUT
//     slot in FB555/IEC_TIMERS_DB (no FB555/DB106 changes needed - that
//     slot no longer needs to be a standalone power-on pulse timer, see
//     next point).
//   - Scale_PowerON_Pulse no longer runs its own separate K2-only
//     pulse - it now enters the SAME ReCalib_Step state machine
//     directly at the Process ON step (3), skipping the power-off+wait
//     - "run Process ON standalone." The old separate "Manual power-on
//     pulse" network is gone; Scale_PowerON_Pulse is checked and
//     cleared inside the main sequence network instead.
//   - Scale_PowerOFF_Pulse (standalone manual power-off) is UNCHANGED -
//     still K2-alone, 3s, fully independent of ReCalib_Step.
//   ReCalib_Step: 0 idle, 1 K2-alone 5s power-off, 2 3s dwell wait
//   (nothing active), 3 Process ON (K1+K2 start together), 4 waiting
//   for K1's 5s hold (started in step 3) to elapse, 5 K1 off,
//   Scale_PowerON_Pulse cleared, done.
//
// v0.29 - per Michou's "Panel LED drive" request (2026-10-05): FC155 no
//   longer drives WHT_SWL_1/2/3_Pnl/RED_LED_Pnl/GRN_LED_Pnl directly -
//   that's now the new standalone/reusable FC157 "PANEL LED DRIVE"
//   (scan fwd/rev, independent, Panic Mode, GRN/RED solid/blink, command
//   bits in new "PANEL LED CMD DB"/DB107, clocks in new FB556/DB108).
//   Removed the old "Lamp scan clock"/"Lamp scan step"/"White lamps"
//   networks (LSIN/LSRS/LSDN/WTON/WSCN/WLDN labels) and the old "Alarm
//   lamps" network; replaced with two short networks that set DB107's
//   command bits to reproduce the exact same old behavior (forward scan
//   while Pump_ON, all three on for Glue_Fill_Pump_Test, solid RED/GRN
//   on any alarm) - then CALLs FC157. No OB1 edit needed, FC157 just
//   rides FC155's existing scan-cycle call. WHT_Panic/GRN_Blink/
//   RED_Blink are left alone here so they stay free for independent/HMI
//   test control - see FC157/DB107 headers. DB105's LampScanStep/
//   LampScanClockMem fields are no longer written by this file -
//   superseded, left declared (see DB105 v0.17).
//
// v0.30 - per Michou (2026-10-06): "need a 30 sec delay (wait) before
//   restarting after power has resumed ... Need to restart KiloTech
//   Scale too and make sure it is calibrated before operating the
//   pump!" Three changes, all gated through OB100 resetting two new
//   DB105 bits every restart (see that file's own changelog):
//   - "Timers" now computes STARTUP_IN as a one-shot latch off
//     PowerUp_Settled (FALSE for exactly the first scan after a
//     restart, TRUE forever after) and calls FB555's new STARTUP_IN/
//     STARTUP_IN_TIME(30s)/STARTUP_OUT - reads as "30s elapsed since
//     the most recent restart," reliably, not a stale carryover (see
//     FB555 v0.4).
//   - "Power-on + calibrate sequence"'s trigger check now ORs in
//     STARTUP_OUT's own rising edge (FP 201.3) alongside the existing
//     Scale_ReCalib_Req edge (FP 201.1) via a new #RC_TRIG temp - so a
//     full recalibration ("restart the scale") auto-runs once, 30s
//     after every restart, same as a manual Scale_ReCalib_Req pulse.
//     RCS5 (sequence done) now also SETs Scale_Calibrated.
//   - NEW "Power-up/recalibration interlock" network (after Overfill/
//     Underfill interlock) blocks Pump_ON while Scale_Calibrated is
//     FALSE (nothing's completed since the last restart yet) or while
//     ReCalib_Step is non-zero (a recalibration is actively running,
//     manual or auto-triggered) - so the pump can't start until the
//     stabilization wait + the full power-off/dwell/Process-ON/hold
//     sequence have all actually completed.
//
// v0.31 - reconciled against Michou's own "Refactor glue scale logic"
//   export (2026-10-06), which was built on v0.29 (not v0.30 - typed
//   into STEP7 before this file's stabilization work existed) and
//   replaced this file's content wholesale. Re-applied v0.30's
//   stabilization logic on top of his real edits below, and adopted his
//   genuine changes: RC_K1HOLD_IN_TIME 5s -> 8s (Process ON's K1 hold is
//   now 8s, not 5s - updates the "~50s" worst-case post-outage pump
//   delay estimate); RCS3 now also clears Scale_ReCalib_Req as soon as
//   Process ON starts, not just on full completion; Alarm lamp command
//   now drives RED_Blink instead of RED_On (alarms blink, don't just
//   light solid); "INPUTS DB".WHT_SW_1_Pump_Test wired to Glue_Fill_
//   Pump_Test (closes one of the "still open" HMI-wiring items - the
//   panel's 3 white lamps/switches are Pump_Test/ReCalib/Alarm_Reset,
//   confirmed by DB60/DB61's own renames in this same export). Also
//   caught and fixed a bug in his retyped "White lamp command" network:
//   the Glue_Fill_Pump_Test branch (WTST) only SET WHT_1, leaving WHT_2/
//   WHT_3 in the CLR group - would have lit only one of the three test
//   lamps instead of all three. Reverted to all three under SET.
//   Added two more switch wirings myself, completing the pattern his
//   own WHT_SW_1_Pump_Test wiring started: "INPUTS DB".WHT_SW_2_ReCalib
//   -> Scale_ReCalib_Req, "INPUTS DB".WHT_SW_3_Alarm_Reset -> Reset_
//   Alarms - closes the other two "still open" HMI-wiring items. Not
//   confirmed by Michou - flag if these two switches are meant for
//   something else.
//
// v0.32 - comment-only: per Michou (2026-10-06): "DB106 Db108 not
//   needed! FB555 Instance is DB555, FB556 Instance is DB556!!!" FB555's
//   instance DB is renumbered DB106 -> DB555, FB556's DB108 -> DB556
//   (each now matches its own FB's number, his preferred convention) -
//   see those files' own changelogs. This file calls both by symbolic
//   name ("IEC TIMERS DB", "SCALE PANEL LAMPS" calls "PANEL LED TIMERS
//   DB" internally), never by number, so no CALL/reference text changed
//   here.
//
// v0.33 - per Michou (2026-10-06): "Need 'PANEL LED CMD DB'.WHT_2 to
//   light up while ReCalib Process." NEW "Recalibration indicator"
//   network: forces WHT_2 (-> WHT_SWL_2_Pnl_Calib, the real Calib lamp)
//   true whenever ReCalib_Step<>0, overriding "White lamp command"
//   above. No explicit off-reset needed - that network's own CLR
//   already zeroes WHT_2 first (Pump_ON is always false while
//   ReCalib_Step<>0, enforced by "Power-up/recalibration interlock").
//   Also confirmed (2026-10-06 report): Michou's own live-retyped copy
//   had two real bugs this tracked source does NOT have - a parameter
//   swap in the "Timers" CALL (RC_K2OFF_IN/RC_K1HOLD_IN crossed, which
//   is exactly why ReCalib_Step was sticking at 1) and WHT_2/WHT_3
//   commented out in WTST (reintroducing the v0.31 bug). Both need
//   fixing by hand in the live project - this file was already correct.
//
// v0.34 - reconciled against Michou's next live update (2026-10-06): he
//   fixed the RC_K2OFF_IN/RC_K1HOLD_IN timer-parameter swap himself
//   (confirms that was indeed the "ReCalib_Step stuck" cause) and
//   upgraded the v0.33 Calib-lamp indicator from a flat SET to mirroring
//   "M 6.5" (a clock-memory bit) while ReCalib_Step<>0 - blinks the lamp
//   instead of solid on. Also added an immediate SET of WHT_2 on
//   #RC_TRIG's own edge, in "Power-on + calibrate sequence" - covers the
//   one scan before ReCalib_Step itself updates, so the lamp turns on
//   with no gap, then the indicator network's blink takes over.
//   NOT adopted: his retyped WTST branch still only SET WHT_1 - the
//   v0.31 bug (WHT_2/WHT_3 never lit during Glue_Fill_Pump_Test) is
//   still present in what he sent, despite the comment there claiming
//   it was fixed. Left this file's own already-correct version
//   (WHT_1/2/3 all under SET) in place - flagged clearly in chat, needs
//   fixing by hand in the live project again.
//
// v0.35 - per Michou (2026-10-06): "Change the comment instead! I want
//   it that way!" - the v0.31 "bug" framing was wrong. WHT_1 only
//   (WHT_SWL_1_Pnl_Pump_Test, its own matching lamp) lighting for
//   Glue_Fill_Pump_Test is INTENTIONAL, not a bug - each white lamp
//   mirrors one specific switch's function (confirmed by DB60/DB61's
//   own renames), so lighting WHT_2/WHT_3 (Calib/Alarm_Reset) during a
//   pump test would be misleading. Reverted WTST to WHT_1 only; updated
//   this network's own header comment and WTST's inline comment to
//   describe the real intent instead of calling it a bug. v0.31's own
//   changelog entry (describing what was believed at the time, before
//   the lamps' individual meanings were known) is left as historical
//   record, not rewritten.
VERSION : 0.35


VAR_TEMP
  RET_VALUE_1 : INT ;	
  RET_VALUE_2 : INT ;	
  CHAR_VALUE : INT ;	
  LOOP_INDEX : INT ;	
  INT_PART : DINT ;	
  FOUND_DIGIT : BOOL ;	
  UPDATE : BOOL ;	
  UNDERFILL_IN : BOOL ;	
  LAMP_IN : BOOL ;	
  RC_K2OFF_IN : BOOL ;	
  RC_GE2 : BOOL ;	
  RC_LE4 : BOOL ;	
  RC_K1HOLD_IN : BOOL ;	
  RC_K2ON_IN : BOOL ;	
  RC_IDLE : BOOL ;	
  RC_WAIT_IN : BOOL ;
  PWROFF_IN : BOOL ;
  STARTUP_IN : BOOL ;
  RC_TRIG : BOOL ;
END_VAR
BEGIN
NETWORK
TITLE =Sync HMI setpoints -> scale setpoints (unconditional, every scan
// Only these fields correspond between "HMI DB" and DB105 - see v0.15/
// v0.18 changelogs for why the other same-offset fields must NOT be
// copied this way.
      L     "HMI DB".Fill_Start_Weight_SP; 
      T     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Fill_Start_SP; 

      L     "HMI DB".Fill_Stop_Weight_SP; 
      T     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Fill_Stop_SP; 

      L     "HMI DB".AlarmLimit_Overfill_SP; 
      T     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".AlarmLimit_Overfill_SP; 

      L     "HMI DB".AlarmLimit_Underfill_SP; 
      T     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".AlarmLimit_Underfill_SP; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Update

      A     "M 6.7"; 
      FP    "FP 201.2"; 
      =     #UPDATE; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Timers - compute each IN condition, CALL FB555 "IEC_TIMERS" once
// FB555 "IEC_TIMERS" (Michou's design, 2026-10-03) wraps all 7 timers
// as multi-instance children of one FB, called once here with one
// instance DB - replacing the earlier design of 7 separate top-level
// SFB4 instance DBs. Each timer is the "TON" library FB (imported from
// the Standard Library after SFB4 failed to resolve on this CPU - see
// v0.26 changelog). Still call-driven, not hardware-autonomous (same
// reasoning as v0.26): every IN condition is recomputed and the whole
// FB is CALLed unconditionally, every scan, regardless of which step is
// active - never gated inside a once-per-step block downstream.
      AN    "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Pump_ON; 
      =     #UNDERFILL_IN; 

      A     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Pump_ON; 
      AN    "IEC TIMERS DB".LAMP_OUT; 
      =     #LAMP_IN; 

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step; 
      L     1; 
      ==I   ; 
      =     #RC_K2OFF_IN; 

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step; 
      L     2; 
      ==I   ; 
      =     #RC_WAIT_IN; 

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step; 
      L     3; 
      >=I   ; 
      =     #RC_GE2; 

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step; 
      L     4; 
      <=I   ; 
      =     #RC_LE4; 

      A     #RC_GE2; 
      A     #RC_LE4; 
      =     #RC_K1HOLD_IN; 

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step; 
      L     3; 
      ==I   ; 
      =     #RC_K2ON_IN; 

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step; 
      L     0; 
      ==I   ; 
      =     #RC_IDLE; 

      A     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Scale_PowerOFF_Pulse;
      A     #RC_IDLE;
      =     #PWROFF_IN;

      A     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".PowerUp_Settled; // FALSE for exactly the first scan after OB100 resets it, TRUE forever after - see DB105/OB100 headers
      =     #STARTUP_IN;
      SET   ;
      S     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".PowerUp_Settled;

      CALL "IEC TIMERS" , "IEC TIMERS DB" (
           LAMP_IN                  := #LAMP_IN,
           LAMP_IN_TIME             := T#500MS,
           UNDERFILL_IN             := #UNDERFILL_IN,
           UNDERFILL_IN_TIME        := T#5S,
           RC_K2OFF_IN              := #RC_K2OFF_IN,
           RC_K2OFF_IN_TIME         := T#5S,
           RC_K1HOLD_IN             := #RC_K1HOLD_IN,
           RC_K1HOLD_IN_TIME        := T#8S,
           RC_K2ON_IN               := #RC_K2ON_IN,
           RC_K2ON_IN_TIME          := T#500MS,
           PWRON_IN                 := #RC_WAIT_IN,
           PWRON_IN_TIME            := T#3S,
           PWROFF_IN                := #PWROFF_IN,
           PWROFF_IN_TIME           := T#3S,
           STARTUP_IN               := #STARTUP_IN,
           STARTUP_IN_TIME          := T#30S);

NETWORK
TITLE =Compute transfered weight and mirror bottomer velocity to HMI DB
// Actual_Transfered_Weight = current weight minus the weight snapshot
// taken at the last pump-start (GrossWeight_Actual_Mem) - see the
// "Pump control" network below for where that snapshot is taken.
// Bottomer_Velocity mirrors the 410 seam-AGC subsystem's own filtered
// web velocity (DB640/"RUN_DATA_DB", owned by FC120/FB610).
      A     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Pump_ON; 
      O     #UPDATE; 
      JCN   UDT0; 

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".GrossWeight_Actual; 
      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".GrossWeight_Actual_Mem; 
      -I    ; 
      T     "HMI DB".Actual_Transfered_Weight; 

      L     "RUN_DATA_DB".Web_Velocity_Filtered; 
      RND   ; 
      T     "HMI DB".Bottomer_Velocity; 

UDT0: NOP   0; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Read 16-BYTE consistent block (IB272-287) via DPRD_DAT

      CALL "DPRD_DAT" (
           LADDR                    := W#16#110,
           RET_VAL                  := #RET_VALUE_1,
           RECORD                   := P#DB4.DBX0.0 BYTE 16);

NETWORK
TITLE =Read 4-BYTE consistent block (IB289-292) via DPRD_DAT

      CALL "DPRD_DAT" (
           LADDR                    := W#16#121,
           RET_VAL                  := #RET_VALUE_2,
           RECORD                   := P#DB4.DBX16.0 BYTE 4);

NETWORK
TITLE =Validate telegram - check RetVal and fixed markers

      L     #RET_VALUE_1; 
      L     0; 
      <>I   ; 
      L     #RET_VALUE_2; 
      L     0; 
      <>I   ; 
      OW    ; 
      L     "ABC3000A_DB".Byte_7; 
      L     B#16#2E; 
      <>I   ; 
      OW    ; 
      L     "ABC3000A_DB".Byte_9; 
      L     B#16#6B; 
      <>I   ; 
      OW    ; 
      L     "ABC3000A_DB".Byte_10; 
      L     B#16#67; 
      <>I   ; 
      OW    ; 
      =     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ParseError; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Parse integer part, Byte_0-5 - LOOP, skip leading spaces until f

      CLR   ; 
      =     #FOUND_DIGIT; 
      L     0; 
      T     #INT_PART; 

      OPN   "ABC3000A_DB"; 
      LAR1  P#0.0; 

      L     6; 
LP1:  T     #LOOP_INDEX; 

      L     DBB [AR1,P#0.0]; 
      L     B#16#20; 
      <>I   ; 
      S     #FOUND_DIGIT; 

      A     #FOUND_DIGIT; 
      JCN   ND1; 

      L     DBB [AR1,P#0.0]; 
      L     B#16#30; 
      -I    ; 
      T     #CHAR_VALUE; 
      L     #INT_PART; 
      L     10; 
      *D    ; 
      L     #CHAR_VALUE; 
      ITD   ; 
      +D    ; 
      T     #INT_PART; 

ND1:  +AR1  P#1.0; 

      L     #LOOP_INDEX; 
      LOOP  LP1; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Parse integer part, Byte_6 - field'S last position, always A dig

      L     "ABC3000A_DB".Byte_6; 
      L     B#16#30; 
      -I    ; 
      T     #CHAR_VALUE; 
      L     #INT_PART; 
      L     10; 
      *D    ; 
      L     #CHAR_VALUE; 
      ITD   ; 
      +D    ; 
      T     #INT_PART; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Store final weight - Byte_8'S decimal digit is discarded, INT re

      L     #INT_PART; 
      T     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".GrossWeight_Actual; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Detect scale fault - GrossWeight_Actual matches the scale'S nega
// Confirmed by Michou: -20663 is the real INT value the KWS CY300
// gives when its reading goes negative. FLAGGED (v0.25): gated on
// #UPDATE only, not every scan unconditionally - confirm intentional.
      O     #UPDATE; 
      JCN   UDT1; 

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".GrossWeight_Actual; 
      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".NegativeUnderScore_Value; 
      ==I   ; 
      S     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Alarm_ScaleFault; 

UDT1: NOP   0; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Platform weight sanity check - GrossWeight_Actual must exceed th
// FLAGGED (v0.25): gated on Pump_ON OR #UPDATE, not every scan -
// confirm intentional.
      A     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Pump_ON; 
      O     #UPDATE; 
      JCN   UDT2; 

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".GrossWeight_Actual; 
      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".PlatformMinWeight_SP; 
      <I    ; 
      S     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Alarm_ScaleFault; 

UDT2: NOP   0; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Mirror parsed weight -> HMI DB (unconditional, for display)

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".GrossWeight_Actual; 
      T     "HMI DB".Actual_Glue_Weight; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Skip valve/alarm update if parse failed or scale fault latched t

      A     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ParseError; 
      O     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Alarm_ScaleFault; 
      JC    SKIP; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Pump control - turns ON below Fill_Start_SP, off at/above Fill_S

      A     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Pump_ON; 
      JC    CHKC; 

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".GrossWeight_Actual; 
      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Fill_Start_SP; 
      <I    ; 
      JC    OPEN; 
      JU    NXT1; 

CHKC: L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".GrossWeight_Actual; 
      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Fill_Stop_SP; 
      >=I   ; 
      JC    CLOS; 
      JU    NXT1; 

OPEN: FP    "FP 201.0"; // edge memory - fires once, the scan Pump_ON is newly commanded on
      JCN   TRXF; 
      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".GrossWeight_Actual; // snapshot weight at pump-start for Actual_Transfered_Weight
      T     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".GrossWeight_Actual_Mem; 

TRXF: SET   ; 
      S     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Pump_ON; 
      JU    NXT1; 

CLOS: SET   ; 
      R     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Pump_ON; 

NXT1: NOP   0; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Overfill alarm - latching, SET ON exceed, no auto-reset here
// FLAGGED (v0.25): gated on Pump_ON OR #UPDATE, not every scan -
// confirm intentional.
      A     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Pump_ON; 
      O     #UPDATE; 
      JCN   NPMP; 

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".GrossWeight_Actual; 
      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".AlarmLimit_Overfill_SP; 
      >I    ; 
      S     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Alarm_Overfill; 

NPMP: NOP   0; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Underfill alarm - latch if weight still below limit after settli
// TON_UNDERFILL's IN is fed from NOT Pump_ON directly (see "Timers"
// network above) - no falling-edge latch needed, TON handles start and
// auto-reset on its own. Pump_ON_Prev is no longer written here
// (DB105 field left declared, unused).
      A     "IEC TIMERS DB".UNDERFILL_OUT; 
      JCN   SKPU; 

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".GrossWeight_Actual; 
      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".AlarmLimit_Underfill_SP; 
      <I    ; 
      S     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Alarm_Underfill; 

SKPU: NOP   0; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Overfill/Underfill interlock - blocks the pump while either is l
// Overfill: an immediate safety stop if weight somehow exceeds the max
// even though Fill_Stop_SP should already have closed the pump.
// Underfill only ever latches after the pump has already stopped, so
// "controls the pump" here means blocking automatic re-engagement, not
// an immediate stop - both read the same way: force Pump_ON off and
// keep it off while either alarm (or Alarm_ScaleFault) is latched,
// until Reset_Alarms clears it.
      A     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Alarm_Overfill;
      O     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Alarm_Underfill;
      O     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Alarm_ScaleFault;
      R     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Pump_ON;

NETWORK
TITLE =Power-up/recalibration interlock - blocks the pump until the scale has completed a recalibration since the last restart
// Scale_Calibrated is reset FALSE by OB100 on every PLC restart (see
// that file) and only SET TRUE once "Power-on + calibrate sequence"
// below completes (RCS5) - so the pump can't run until the scale has
// actually been recalibrated since the last power-up. Also blocks it
// while ReCalib_Step is non-zero (any recalibration actively running,
// manual or the v0.30 auto-trigger), not just right after a restart.
      AN    "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Scale_Calibrated;
      R     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Pump_ON;

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step;
      L     0;
      <>I   ;
      R     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Pump_ON;

NETWORK
TITLE =Exit point for parse-error skip

SKIP: NOP   0; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Alarm reset switch -> Reset_Alarms (completes Michou's WHT_SW_1_Pump_Test wiring pattern, v0.31, not yet confirmed)

      A     "INPUTS DB".WHT_SW_3_Alarm_Reset;
      =     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Reset_Alarms;

NETWORK
TITLE =Reset latched alarms - HMI-driven, runs regardless OF this scan'

      A     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Reset_Alarms;
      R     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Alarm_Overfill; 
      R     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Alarm_Underfill; 
      R     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Alarm_ScaleFault; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Drive physical glue pump output - automatic Pump_ON, Glue_Fill_P

      A     "INPUTS DB".WHT_SW_1_Pump_Test; 
      =     "HMI DB".Glue_Fill_Pump_Test; 
//;
      A     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Pump_ON; 
      O     "HMI DB".Glue_Fill_Pump_Test; 
      =     "HMI DB".Glue_Fill_Pump_ON; 

NETWORK
TITLE =White lamp command -> PANEL LED CMD DB (FC158)
// Reproduces the old directly-driven behavior (forward scan while
// Pump_ON, WHT_1 only for Glue_Fill_Pump_Test, off otherwise) via
// FC158's command interface instead of touching WHT_SWL_1/2/3_Pnl here.
// v0.35 (Michou, 2026-10-06 - "Change the comment instead! I want it
// that way!"): confirmed intentional - WHT_1 is WHT_SWL_1_Pnl_Pump_Test,
// its OWN matching lamp, not a generic "test in progress" indicator for
// all three. Lighting WHT_2/WHT_3 (Calib/Alarm_Reset) too would be
// misleading, now that each white lamp mirrors a specific switch's
// function. Retracts the v0.31 "bug" framing - that was based on the
// older assumption (all three as one undifferentiated scan group),
// before DB60/DB61's own renames revealed the real per-lamp meaning.
      A     "HMI DB".Glue_Fill_Pump_Test;
      JC    WTST;

      A     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Pump_ON;
      =     "PANEL LED CMD DB".WHT_ScanFwd;
      CLR   ;
      =     "PANEL LED CMD DB".WHT_ScanRev;
      =     "PANEL LED CMD DB".WHT_1;
      =     "PANEL LED CMD DB".WHT_2;
      =     "PANEL LED CMD DB".WHT_3;
      JU    WCDN;

WTST: CLR   ; // Intentional: WHT_2/WHT_3 stay off here - only WHT_1 (its own matching lamp) lights for Glue_Fill_Pump_Test, see this network's header
      =     "PANEL LED CMD DB".WHT_ScanFwd;
      =     "PANEL LED CMD DB".WHT_ScanRev;
      =     "PANEL LED CMD DB".WHT_2;
      =     "PANEL LED CMD DB".WHT_3;

      SET   ;
      =     "PANEL LED CMD DB".WHT_1;

WCDN: NOP   0;

NETWORK
TITLE =Recalibration indicator - WHT_2 (Calib lamp) blinks while ReCalib_Step is active
// Overrides "White lamp command" above: WHT_2 is "PANEL LED CMD DB".
// WHT_2 -> WHT_SWL_2_Pnl_Calib - the recalibration indicator lamp
// (confirmed by DB60/DB61's own naming - see FC155's v0.31 changelog).
// Pump_ON is already blocked whenever ReCalib_Step<>0 (see "Power-up/
// recalibration interlock" above), so the network above always clears
// WHT_2 to FALSE first (idle/independent branch) before this runs - no
// explicit reset needed here, just drive it while recalibrating.
// v0.34 (Michou, 2026-10-06): mirrors "M 6.5" (a clock-memory bit) while
// active, instead of a flat SET - blinks the lamp instead of solid on.
// Not independently confirmed that M6.5 is configured as a clock memory
// bit in HW config - flag if it isn't, this would just read as a static
// bit value instead of blinking. The "Power-on + calibrate sequence"
// network below also SETs WHT_2 once, on the same scan a recalibration
// is actually triggered (RC_TRIG's edge) - covers the one scan before
// ReCalib_Step itself updates to 1, so the lamp turns on immediately
// with no gap, then this network takes over the blink from the next
// scan once ReCalib_Step<>0 is true.
      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step;
      L     0;
      <>I   ;
      JCN   RCWD;

      A     "M 6.5";
      =     "PANEL LED CMD DB".WHT_2;

RCWD: NOP   0;

NETWORK
TITLE =Recalibration switch -> Scale_ReCalib_Req (one-shot per press, v0.31, not yet confirmed)
// NOT a level-mirror like the Pump_Test wiring above - RCS3 (below)
// explicitly R's Scale_ReCalib_Req once Process ON starts, so a
// continuous mirror of a still-held switch would just re-assert it
// right back the very next scan and defeat that clear. SETs once per
// switch rising edge (FP 201.4) instead; the sequence/FP 201.1 below
// clear it again for the next press.
      A     "INPUTS DB".WHT_SW_2_ReCalib;
      FP    "FP 201.4";
      S     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Scale_ReCalib_Req;

NETWORK
TITLE =Power-on + calibrate sequence ("Process ON" = K1+K2 simultaneous
// KWS CY300 power-up defect workaround: the scale resets its zero/
// calibration reference every power-up. Corrected sequence (Michou,
// 2026-10-03 - supersedes the earlier K1-then-K2 design):
//   "Process ON": K1 and K2 start SIMULTANEOUSLY - K2 pulses 0.5s, K1
//   stays on for a flat 5s. This is the shared building block used both
//   by a full recalibration (after powering off) and by a standalone
//   manual power-on.
//   Full recalibration: K2 ALONE (no K1) for 5s (power off) -> wait 3s
//   with nothing active -> Process ON.
//   Scale_PowerON_Pulse now enters this same state machine directly at
//   the Process ON step (3), skipping the power-off+wait - "run Process
//   ON standalone." Auto-clears when Process ON completes (step 5).
//   Scale_PowerOFF_Pulse remains fully independent (separate network
//   below, unchanged - still K2-alone 3s, not part of this state
//   machine at all).
//   ReCalib_Step: 0 idle, 1 K2-alone 5s power-off (RC_K2OFF_OUT), 2 3s
//   dwell wait with nothing active (reuses the PWRON_IN/PWRON_OUT timer
//   slot in FB555/IEC TIMERS DB - no longer a standalone power-on pulse
//   timer, repurposed here since Scale_PowerON_Pulse no longer needs
//   its own separate timer), 3 Process ON: K1 on + K2 0.5s pulse BOTH
//   START THIS STEP (RC_K2ON_OUT and RC_K1HOLD_OUT both begin here), 4
//   waiting for RC_K1HOLD_OUT's 8s (which started back in step 3) to
//   elapse, 5 K1 off, Scale_PowerON_Pulse cleared, done.
      A     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Scale_ReCalib_Req;
      FP    "FP 201.1";
      =     #RC_TRIG;

      A     "IEC TIMERS DB".STARTUP_OUT; // auto-trigger a full recalibration once, 30s after every restart - "restart the scale" (Michou, 2026-10-06)
      FP    "FP 201.3";
      O     #RC_TRIG;
      =     #RC_TRIG;

      A     #RC_TRIG;
      S     "PANEL LED CMD DB".WHT_2; // immediate on, same scan the trigger fires - closes the 1-scan gap before ReCalib_Step updates and the "Recalibration indicator" network above takes over
      JCN   RCCH;

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step;
      L     0;
      <>I   ;
      JC    RCCH;

      L     1;
      T     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step;

RCCH: A     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Scale_PowerON_Pulse;
      JCN   RCST; 

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step; 
      L     0; 
      <>I   ; 
      JC    RCST; 

      L     3; 
      T     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step; 

RCST: L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step; 
      L     1; 
      ==I   ; 
      JC    RCS1; 

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step; 
      L     2; 
      ==I   ; 
      JC    RCS2; 

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step; 
      L     3; 
      ==I   ; 
      JC    RCS3; 

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step; 
      L     4; 
      ==I   ; 
      JC    RCS4; 

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step; 
      L     5; 
      ==I   ; 
      JC    RCS5; 
      JU    RCDN; 

RCS1: SET   ; 
      S     "OUTPUTS DB".KILOTECK_Power_K2; // K2 alone, 5s power-off

      A     "IEC TIMERS DB".RC_K2OFF_OUT; 
      JCN   RCDN; 
      R     "OUTPUTS DB".KILOTECK_Power_K2; 
      L     2; 
      T     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step; 
      JU    RCDN; 

RCS2: A     "IEC TIMERS DB".PWRON_OUT; // repurposed: 3s dwell wait, nothing driven
      JCN   RCDN; 
      L     3; 
      T     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step; 
      JU    RCDN; 

RCS3: SET   ; 
      S     "OUTPUTS DB".KILOTECK_Calib_K1; // Process ON: K1 + K2 start together
      SET   ; 
      S     "OUTPUTS DB".KILOTECK_Power_K2; 

      A     "IEC TIMERS DB".RC_K2ON_OUT; // 8 sec Hold
      JCN   RCDN; 
      R     "OUTPUTS DB".KILOTECK_Power_K2; 
      R     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Scale_ReCalib_Req; 
      L     4; 
      T     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step; 
      JU    RCDN; 

RCS4: A     "IEC TIMERS DB".RC_K1HOLD_OUT; 
      JCN   RCDN; 
      L     5; 
      T     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step; 
      JU    RCDN; 

RCS5: SET   ;
      R     "OUTPUTS DB".KILOTECK_Calib_K1;
      CLR   ;
      =     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Scale_PowerON_Pulse;
      L     0;
      T     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step;
      SET   ;
      S     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Scale_Calibrated;

RCDN: NOP   0;

NETWORK
TITLE =Manual power-off pulse - 3S K2 pulse ON Scale_PowerOFF_Pulse, au
// TON_PWR_OFF's IN (Scale_PowerOFF_Pulse AND ReCalib_Step=0) is
// computed and CALLed every scan in "Timers" above - this network just
// drives K2 and reads .Q. Unlike the old design, Scale_PowerON_Pulse no
// longer has a matching standalone network here - it enters the
// "Power-on + calibrate sequence" network above directly, since
// standalone power-on now means running "Process ON", which needs K1
// too.
      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ReCalib_Step; 
      L     0; 
      <>I   ; 
      JC    PFDN; 

      A     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Scale_PowerOFF_Pulse; 
      JCN   PFDN; 

      SET   ; 
      S     "OUTPUTS DB".KILOTECK_Power_K2; 

      A     "IEC TIMERS DB".PWROFF_OUT; 
      JCN   PFDN; 
      R     "OUTPUTS DB".KILOTECK_Power_K2; 
      CLR   ; 
      =     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Scale_PowerOFF_Pulse; 

PFDN: NOP   0; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Alarm lamp command -> PANEL LED CMD DB (FC157 drives the physica
// Extends beyond just Overfill/Underfill to include Alarm_ScaleFault.
      A     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Alarm_Overfill; 
      O     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Alarm_Underfill; 
      O     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Alarm_ScaleFault; 
      =     "PANEL LED CMD DB".RED_Blink; 

      NOT   ; 
      =     "PANEL LED CMD DB".GRN_On; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Drive Panel LED outputs - CALL FC157 "PANEL LED DRIVE" once, eve

      CALL "SCALE PANEL LAMPS" ;

END_FUNCTION

